/! Challenge
section#challenge.challenge
  .container
	.row.align-items-center.g-5
	  .col-lg-5
		h2 The challenge

		p.lead.text-mb-5
		  | United Way of Central Maryland needed a redesigned website that made it easier for visitors to explore programs, access community resources, and engage with the organization's mission. While the visual direction had been established, the initial development effort struggled to translate the approved designs into a functional, responsive, and optimized WordPress experience.

		p.lead
		  | Drio Duo brought me into the project to help overcome these implementation challenges and move the website forward. The work required balancing design fidelity, usability, performance, and the flexibility needed to manage a content-rich nonprofit website.
		p.lead As the project evolved, an additional challenge emerged: incorporating United Way's updated national branding into the regional website while maintaining consistency across existing pages and future design initiatives.

	  .col-lg-7
		= link_to image_path("portfolio/community-impact-website/communityimpact-before-after.jpg"), "data-fancybox"=>"gallery", "data-caption"=>"A comparison of the homepage before and after the redesign, highlighting updated branding, a more engaging visual experience, and improved content organization." do
			= image_tag "portfolio/community-impact-website/communityimpact-before-after.jpg", :class=>"img-fluid w-100 h-auto border border-2 border-dark rounded-3 box-shadow", :alt=>"Community Impact Website Before & After"
		p.small.text-center.mt-3.mb-0
		  | Before and after: A refreshed homepage with updated branding, improved visual hierarchy, and clearer pathways to community resources.

/! Approach
section#approach
